---
description: Review code for correctness, safety, and maintainability
argument-hint: "[scope]"
---
Review {{ arguments | default("the current changes", true) }}.

Work from the actual code and tests. Check correctness first, followed by edge
cases, error handling, security, concurrency, performance, compatibility, and
test coverage. Keep style comments low priority.

Report findings in severity order with file and line references. For each
finding, explain the problem, its impact, and a practical fix. Mark downstream
effects as unverified when the available evidence cannot prove them. End with a
short note about choices that are working well. If there are no findings, say
so directly.
